this conference will take place in the  margins of the justice and Home Affairs  Council it will focus on the important  increase in the number of migrants  coming from the middle east through the  Western Balkans world it will aim to  enhance the engagement among your  partners increase in solidarity and also  ensuring an orderly management of the  refugee and migrant flows there will be  some key areas of discussion there will  be a discussion on how to increase  support to Jordan Lebanon and Turkey  which are the first countries of asylum  then there will be a discussion on how  to support all the affected transit  countries how they can improve reception  registration and Asylum procedures and  the third one will be enhancing the  cooperation to fight organized crime  were responsible for the migrant  smuggling and in trafficking in human  beings the high-level conference aims  also to engage with the countries of  origin of irregular migrants and also to  address the root causes of the forced  displacement
 

